	abstract = {It is found that a proposed random number generator ran2, previously presented, see ibid. vol. 6, 521-4 (1992), is a good one, but a number of generators are presented that are at least as good and are simpler, much faster, and with periods \{\&\}ldquo;billions and billions\{\&\}rdquo; of times longer. They are presented not necessarily to supplant ran2, but to put it in perspective. Any serious user of Monte Carlo methods should have a variety of random number generators from which to choose. In addition to two specific programs, one in Fortran and one in C, a framework is offered within which the readers can easily fashion their own generators with periods ranging from 10$^{\textrm{27}}$-10$^{\textrm{101}}$},
