	abstract = {A legislative body is a large human group. As a large group it tends to be characterized by the development of informal sub-groups consisting of individuals who interact on a persistent and uniform basis. This informal organization of the legislative group functions as an intervening system in the decision-making process. A careful analysis of the patterns of informal organization and interpersonal relations in a state legislative group is provided by a recent study of the Wisconsin State Assembly. © 1959 Princeton University.},
