	abstract = {The minimum wage is a policy commonly used in both advanced and emerging market economies to support the wages of low-wage workers and to increase the income of the poor. However, the efficacy of the minimum wage as a policy tool is controversial. Although minimum wages do raise the wages of low-skilled workers, they also reduce employment opportunities for such workers and raise the prices of goods and services produced with low-wage labor. On balance, minimum wages appear to have little, if any, beneficial effect on the distribution of income.},
